The contrast is action based on a belief, conclusion, idea, or formula: $\hbox{belief/conclusion/idea}
\Rightarrow
\hbox{time-binding action}
\Rightarrow
\hbox{conflict and sorrow}.$ Time-binding here means bound to interval: postponement, succession, regret, and consequence. The action begins from a formula; the formula belongs to knowledge; knowledge belongs to the past. The past then acts under the name of present action.

