A useful reconstruction is $\begin{aligned}
\hbox{direct seeing} &\Rightarrow \hbox{no interval},\\
\hbox{idea-based action} &\Rightarrow \hbox{interval and conflict}.\end{aligned}$ The distinction is local and precise. Krishnamurti is not saying that practical knowledge has no place. He is saying that when psychological action is based on an idea, it carries division and time into the action itself.

