We can write the ordinary movement as an update sequence: $\hbox{statement heard}
\to
\hbox{words}
\to
\hbox{conclusion}
\to
\hbox{idea}
\to
\hbox{problem of carrying it out}.$ This is the chapter’s cleanest local mechanism. The mind has not stayed with the statement. It has converted the statement into its own abstraction. Once different minds carry different abstractions, conflict follows naturally.

