p.src:
Attention is now the center of the inquiry. Krishnamurti says that attention means no border. The moment there is a frontier, the mind begins to fight, agree, disagree, compare, and form concepts. We may record the border condition as $\hbox{frontier in attention}
\Rightarrow
\hbox{concept, comparison, resistance}.$ The absence of frontier is not vagueness. It is the condition in which the mind is not divided from what is being heard.

