p.src:
That is why the question How shall I maintain attention? is already suspect. It asks for a method that will secure a return: $\hbox{practice attention}
\to
\hbox{obtain reward}.$ But Krishnamurti says attention is not a result. It has no cause in the reward-seeking sense. What has a cause has an effect, and the effect becomes a further cause. That is a circle, while attention does not belong to that circle.

